+# Genesis P4 — organism renderer and reachable lab
+
+Implemented on branch `new`, after local P3 `e1035297d3386de5a0949d905892283342fca633`.
+User explicitly authorized work through P4 without intermediate APK testing.
+Final milestone message: `mdna(genesis-p4): organism renderer`. Exact hash is in
+Git and the ZIP delivery record. P5 has not started.
+
+## What is reachable
+
+**Now Playing -> Visualizer -> Open MDNA Genesis**. This entry and DnaLabScreen
+are in `main`, available to release builds without a debug flag. Back returns to
+the existing Visualizer Lab; the overlay back-handler order now allows this
+nested screen to consume Back first. Playback uses the existing PlayerViewModel
+play/pause action. No second player, new permission, cloud service or static
+reference-image background was introduced.
+
+Opening a song loads its cached Room DNA profile, or analyzes it off the UI thread
+through P2's shared/cancellable decoder. Leaving/stopping the screen cancels the
+analysis. An immediate P0 live orb remains available while analysis runs or fails.
+The complete result is mapped using P1 and inserted once through P3, then published
+as immutable render parameters. Track changes clear the previous genome before
+loading the next. URI/size/modified-time hash is only a local cache key; base DNA
+still derives from decoded audio and canonical musical features.
+
+## Rendering architecture
+
+- `DnaOrganism` owns the existing lifecycle-aware GLSurfaceView host. Choreographer
+  requests frames; the GL thread samples interpolated live spectrum and updates
+  uniforms, independently of ordinary Compose recomposition. UI diagnostics poll
+  at 2 Hz. Actual sample rate is forwarded to the band grouping.
+- Orb: layered, continuously deformed latitude spirals and fine luminous points.
+  Terrain: connected serpentine contour ribbons, waves and spectral-energy peaks.
+  Nebula: layered flowing particle formations with localized transient response.
+  Seed, chroma distribution, symmetry, brightness, deformation, density, layers,
+  flow, sharpness and microdetail produce variations within these families.
+- Shared ESSL 3.00 geometry is generated by gl_VertexID. No mesh regeneration or
+  vertex upload per frame. Uniform arrays and matrix buffers are reused; programs
+  and locations are cached. Failed programs are not recompiled every frame.
+- Bass expands geometry, mids deform surfaces, treble changes fine detail and
+  brightness, and live beat envelope drives genome-scaled transient response.
+  Cyan/blue/violet colour transitions remain spatially coherent.
+- Quality controls retain automatic downgrade protection. Low/Mid/High scene
+  framebuffer scales are 0.6/0.8/1.0; targets are recreated only on size/tier
+  changes. Point budgets are row-aligned, capped at 32,736 per layer and 163,680
+  total. These are limits, **not measured device performance**. Optional bloom
+  failure uses direct GLES rendering. GLES <3.0 reports unsupported while playback
+  continues. API 26–32 uses the same GLES 3 path; no RuntimeShader dependency.
+- Renderer lifecycle, GPU cleanup/context-loss handling and manual route-specific
+  AV offset are retained. Freeze-motion control and the system animator-disabled
+  preference reduce motion; playback pause stops the motion clock. P0's separate
+  API-33 AGSL debug atmosphere remains intact, not relabeled as GLES shader code.
+- Standalone debug template cycling skips genome-only shaders, preventing blank
+  uninitialized scenes. Existing basic drag/pinch support is retained; P5's full
+  interaction, inertia, pulse/haptics/accessibility work is not claimed.
+
+## Validation actually performed
+
+| Check | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| P1 production Java + independent Python golden oracle | 17 JVM groups and all 3 goldens PASS |
+| P2 production analyzer, synthetic fixtures, 64 MB test heap | 13 JVM groups PASS |
+| Actual checked-in ESSL compile/link on surfaceless Mesa | PASS; legacy shader pairs also compile |
+| 3 families x 2 parameter variations | 6 visible distinct renders; repeated identical inputs reproduce pixels on this renderer |
+| Independent bass, mid and treble changes | All 18 response comparisons change rendered pixels |
+| 375x812 / 812x375, all 3 tiers and families, full-scale audio | 18 render cases PASS; visible geometry within viewport |
+| Workflow YAML, Git whitespace and credential-pattern scan | PASS at milestone preparation |
+| Android Gradle, release assembly, instrumentation compile | BLOCKED before Gradle launch; wrapper download: Network is unreachable |
+| Android Room migration and renderer instrumentation execution | NOT RUN; no Android SDK/device/emulator |
+
+`tools/organism_shader_probe.py --animation` reproduces six PNGs, machine-readable
+checks and a three-second synthetic-input orb GIF in `evidence/`. These are actual
+ESSL renders on Mesa software GL, **not Android UI screenshots, live song captures,
+AGSL validation, physical-GPU results or a phone FPS benchmark**. Pixel equivalence
+is scoped to this renderer; cross-GPU bit-identical pixels are not guaranteed.
+
+New `DnaRenderStateTest` covers 256 seeded genomes, all families, quality bounds,
+serialization-to-render identity, silent chroma and safe standalone cycling. Added
+Android renderer coverage for all families/tiers across recreated contexts. CI now
+selects renderer/core JUnit tests and compiles all Android test sources. Added
+`kspAndroidTest` for the genuine Room-v5 fixture implementation and strengthened
+its regression to preserve every field of seeded playlists, membership, favorites,
+history, EQ settings/presets, waveform cache and playback state. **These new Kotlin,
+Room and Android tests are written but unexecuted locally.**
+
+## Limits and next gate
+
+- No P3/P4 APK, successful new CI run, device screenshot, measured frame pacing,
+  audio-glitch result, thermal/battery observation or leak measurement exists here.
+  GitHub writes were previously denied; no push or history rewrite was attempted.
+- Offline summary + genome + live reactive rendering are connected. The P2 feature
+  timeline is not yet persisted or fused with live input. Full Hybrid Option C
+  playback-position/output-timing controller remains outstanding before production
+  integration/export; the current hub uses a latency estimate and manual offset.
+  No one-frame synchronization guarantee is made.
+- P3 meaningful-listen query excludes zero-duration track-start events; the existing
+  history writer still needs P6 duration accumulation. Unsupported pre-v2 databases
+  fail safely after destructive fallback removal. Real-user v5 fixture validation
+  remains outstanding; the instrumentation fixture is generated by Room v5.
+- First analysis latency, decoder compatibility, analysis/playback contention,
+  repeated navigation, rotation/background/resume and Bluetooth changes need real
+  Android verification. Largest font sizes, TalkBack and physical small-screen UI
+  layout have not been exercised. Shader aspect tests do not validate Compose UI.
+- Source remains at P4. P5 is ready for implementation after this renderer/build
+  review; any build or visual defect should be resolved before calling it validated.
+
+Full changed-file inventory: `P4_FILES.txt`. P3 storage report: `P3_REPORT.md`.
